-- Step 8: attributes. #[key = value, flag, ...] goes on the line before ANY symbol:
-- constant, structure, enum, type, function and implementation. An attribute line has no ";".
-- A key without a value means "= true". A key that is not an enum key takes true or false.
-- A key of an enum takes one member of that enum: inline = force, build = debug.
-- Visibility is an attribute. There is no public or local keyword.
-- The key visibility is an enum key with the members public and private.
--   #[visibility = public]   other files can import the symbol
--   #[visibility = private]  only this file can use it. This is the default, so it can be left out.
-- visibility twice on one symbol is an error. An unknown key is an error.

namespace attributes.visibility;

#[visibility = public]
constant VERSION: sinteger32 = 1;

#[visibility = private]
constant SECRET: sinteger32 = 42;

constant ALSO_PRIVATE: sinteger32 = 43;

function hidden(): sinteger32
    return ALSO_PRIVATE;
end

#[visibility = public]
function visible(): sinteger32
    return hidden() + SECRET;
end
